  "lineage": "Central Javanese hybrid popularised from the early 1990s by Manthous and his Orkes Campursari Gunung Kidul, building on 1960s experiments by RM Samsi — literally 'mixed essence', it sets langgam Jawa and keroncong melodies over a pelog/slendro-tuned electronic keyboard doubling saron and gender parts, with kendang leading the tempo, siter and suling ornamenting, bass guitar walking under, at a relaxed 90–110 BPM behind a sinden-derived Javanese vocal using narrow ornamented cengkok phrasing.",
